  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to simplify the given product of logarithmic terms. Let's break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, recall the change of base formula for logarithms:\n\\[\n\\log_a b = \\frac{\\log_c b}{\\log_c a}\n\\]\nwhere \\(c\\) is any positive number.\n\nFor our problem, we have:\n\\[\n\\prod_{k=4}^{63} \\frac{\\log_k(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_{k+1}(5^{k^2-4})}\n\\]\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we can rewrite each term in the product as follows:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\log_k(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_{k+1}(5^{k^2-4})} = \\frac{\\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1})}{\\log_5 k}}{\\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4})}{\\log_5 (k+1)}} = \\frac{\\log_5(5^{k^2-1}) \\cdot \\log_5 (k+1)}{\\log_5(5^{k^2-4}) \\cdot \\log_5 k}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further using the property of logarithms \\(\\log_a b^c = c \\log_a b\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{(k^2-1) \\log_5 (k+1)}{(k^2-4) \\log_5 k}\n\\]\n\nNow, let's substitute the values of \\(k\\) from 4 to 63 and notice that many terms will cancel out:\n\\[\n\\frac{(4^2-1) \\log_5 (5)}{(4^2-4) \\log_5 4} \\cdot \\frac{(5^2-1) \\log_5 (6)}{(5^2-4) \\log_5 5} \\cdot \\frac{(6^2-1) \\log_5 (7)}{(6^2-4) \\log_5 6} \\cdots \\frac{(63^2-1) \\log_5 (64)}{(63^2-4) \\log_5 63}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 \\log_5 1}{12 \\log_5 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\log_5 6}{21 \\log_5 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\log_5 7}{32 \\log_5 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\log_5 64}{3965 \\log_5 63}\n\\]\n\nNotice that most terms will cancel out, leaving us with:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 \\log_5 64}{12 \\log_5 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\log_5 6}{21 \\log_5 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\log_5 7}{32 \\log_5 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\log_5 64}{3965 \\log_5 63}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies further to:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 \\cdot 6}{12 \\cdot 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\cdot 6}{21 \\cdot 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\cdot 7}{32 \\cdot 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\cdot 64}{3965 \\cdot 63}\n\\]\n\nThe final simplified form is:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 \\cdot 6}{12 \\cdot 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\cdot 6}{21 \\cdot 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\cdot 7}{32 \\cdot 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\cdot 64}{3965 \\cdot 63} = \\frac{15 \\cdot 6}{12 \\cdot 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\cdot 6}{21 \\cdot 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\cdot 7}{32 \\cdot 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\cdot 64}{3965 \\cdot 63}\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{15 \\cdot 6}{12 \\cdot 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\cdot 6}{21 \\cdot 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\cdot 7}{32 \\cdot 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\cdot 64}{3965 \\cdot 63} = \\frac{15 \\cdot 6}{12 \\cdot 4} \\cdot \\frac{24 \\cdot 6}{21 \\cdot 5} \\cdot \\frac{35 \\cdot 7}{32 \\cdot 6} \\cdots \\frac{3968 \\cdot 64}{3965 \\cdot 63}\n\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{15}\n\\]",
